# Rianell UI motion standards

## Performance constraints (non-negotiable)

- Animate only **`transform`**, **`opacity`**, and **`filter`** — GPU-bound only
- Never animate `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, or `padding` — these force layout
- The main thread must stay free for Supabase sync and on-device AI inference

## Animation tokens (PWA)

- Boot skeleton delays use the existing CSS custom property ladder in `styles.css`
- Tab transitions: `ai-animate-in` nth-child stagger, shimmer timing already defined in `styles.css`
- Bottom-nav icon lift: use the existing `.bottom-nav__icon--lift` class
- Reduced motion: always gate new animations with `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` or the `reducedMotion` pref

## Loading / AI states

- Never show a bare spinner during LLM inference — use skeleton loaders with `bioluminescent-shimmer` timing
- Transition from loading → insight revealed must be a staggered `ai-animate-in` reveal sequence
- AI Synthesis state: characters morph/ripple via CSS `clip-path` or `transform: scaleY()` only

## React Native (RN)

- Motion utilities: `PrimaryButton`, `Skeleton`, `Toast`, `EmptyState`, `HomeWelcomeCard`, `SettingsChapter` already have motion applied
- Screen stagger/slide implemented on AI, Charts, Mood, and Log Wizard screens — match this pattern for new screens
- RTL: always check `isRtl` for directional animations (chevron mirroring, slide direction)

## Design philosophy

- Whimsical but never clinical — health stats should feel alive, not like a spreadsheet
- Milestone achievements trigger micro-celebrations (particle burst, card shimmer) — use existing toast queue
- Security feedback (auth, encryption) uses a concentric ripple pattern on confirmation
